Kind: ablation
Issue: #934
Takes out: the read of a task's usage before proc_server ends it for a signal -- terminate_for_signal() calls task_terminate() with the usage unread, and once the task is gone it cannot be asked: musl_test's [49] must see wait4() give a child killed by SIGKILL after 600 ms of spinning no time
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: musl_test: \[49\] WRONG -- .*its time NOT there

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/proc_server/proc_main.c b/uros/src/servers/proc_server/proc_main.c
index e0f08e1d..89498010 100644
--- a/uros/src/servers/proc_server/proc_main.c
+++ b/uros/src/servers/proc_server/proc_main.c
@@ -1091,8 +1091,7 @@ terminate_for_signal(proc_pid_t pid, int signo, mach_port_t task)
         e->exit_declared = 1;
     }
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&pid_lock);
-    /* #934: its usage while it can still be asked, for wait4()'s rusage. */
-    refresh_rusage_for_pid(pid);
+    /* 934-kill-time-unread: the task goes with its usage unread */
     return task_terminate(task);
 }
 
